Maria Chen: opened a tiny PR to add a Python SDK example for envelope normalization + a short parse shim. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/907

Andre Gomez: excellent — most examples are JS, a Python one will help. Keep it minimal, show requests + stream fallback.

Maria Chen: draft Python snippet:
```python
# sync parse shim
def normalize(resp):
    try:
        return json.loads(resp)
    except Exception:
        return {"text": str(resp)}

# streaming: yield chunks, stop on parse error
for chunk in client.stream(model, prompt):
    try:
        yield json.loads(chunk)
    except Exception:
        client.cancel_stream()
        yield {"text": accumulated}
        break
```

Priya Sharma: add a tiny JSON schema for union types where items can be string or object. folks get confused with unions in arrays:
```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "entries": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": { "type": ["string", "object"] }
    }
  }
}
```

